son have turned into a  ruthless pair who terrorizes the town  and takes pleasure in crippling anyone  who offends them one day the father-son  duo accompanied by their lead bodyguard  juan arrives at a tavern there chang and  juan unjustly beat up two men who look  at them the wrong way seeing this the  town's blacksmith way becomes horrified  and loudly berates them for bullying the  man after wei leaves tientu plots with  juan to teach him a lesson later  meanwhile a traveling salesman named  chen also speaks out against the  family's barbaric actions the statement  greatly upsets chang prompting him to  approach and attack the salesman chen  doesn't get a chance to react as chang  swiftly uses his iron fists to poke  chen's eyes permanently blinding the  traveler as he stumbles to the floor in  pain in the following scene tien 2 sends  juan along with his other bodyguards to  bring the town's blacksmith way to his  mansion at the mansion way is instantly  seized by the guards and forced to drink  a strange liquid as a result he loses  his voice permanently devastated way  curses tien 2 by writing an inscription  on a nearby table sadly this bold action  pisses tien 2 off and he fiercely slaps  wei's ears making him deaf as well the  next day tientu and chang accompanied by  their entourage take a stroll around  town a man named akui mistakenly bumps  into chiang which causes the two men to  argue an abusive chang throws akui to  the ground and orders his bodyguards to  cut off akui's legs in the next scene  chang's disabled victims discover each  other and are bullied by some villagers  fortunately this doesn't last long as a  visiting kung fu master named yi comes  to their aid and chases the bullies away  yi also learns if tu's tyranny and  promises to avenge the cripples as he  swiftly walks to the master's mansion  there he meets tien2 alongside his  entourage and condemns the fighter's  violent actions his words prompt two of  tiantu's bodyguards to attack him but he  easily takes them down after a while the  lead bodyguard juan charges at yi and  the duo engages in a fierce battle  eventually chang joins the fight and  manages to capture yi with juan's help  tientu's men torture ye using an iron  vice to compress his skull sadly the  punishment results in ye suffering  severe brain damage making him mentally  disabled man life sure makes you  aggressive when you can't touch yourself  after this ye is thrown out of the  mansion and left to die luckily he is  helped by the other three cripples who  rescue him and take him to way's shop  the cripples ask ye multiple questions  to determine where he comes from however  a now idiotic yi merely jumps around  playfully right then akui searches yi  and finds a note from his teacher who  lives at a nearby kung fu school  learning this the four disabled men  embark on a journey to return yee to his  master wei uses a barrow to transport a  blind chen and a crippled akui while yee  fools around behind them eventually the  men arrive at the school but find its  doors tightly shot yi easily scales the  fence and enters the compound opening  the doors for the rest from the inside  the disabled men find yee's master jin  ying and tell the aged man about  tiantu's tyranny and his numerous  violent actions leading to their  respective disabilities jin ying is  horrified by the news and reveals that  tientu was once a hero who used his  fighting skills for good however he is  now turned into a monster after the  assassins attacked his home many years  ago the master thanks the cripples for  returning ye and to show his  appreciation offers to teach them kung  fu the men are ecstatic to hear this and  quickly accept the offer as they plan to  enact their revenge on tien ii and take  the tyrant down the next day jin yang  commences their training and uses a  unique teaching style for each man in  line with their disabilities he  instructs wei to make a pair of  prosthetic iron legs for akui after a  long day's work the blacksmith  successfully makes them and akui tries  them on he isn't used to the artificial  legs and shakily stands on his feet  before falling to the ground jin yang  also trains chen to use his sense of  hearing to supplement his lack of sight  chen learns to sharpen his ears and  eventually masters using them over time  chen is able to accurately shoot down  several falling leaves by just using his  keen hearing later the master teaches  way alongside the others a unique palm  sign language to communicate with the  deaf man jing ying uses the technique to  deliver multiple instructions to wei and  teaches him martial arts tricks such as  using reflective bands to see objects or  opponents moving behind him meanwhile  akui practices walking on the prosthetic  legs and gradually perfects using them  he also learns kung fu kicks and uses  his powerful metal legs to his advantage  on the other hand wang yi though  mentally disabled remains a skilled  martial arts master hence he requires no  further teaching he spends the entire  time mindlessly disturbing the other  cripples and occasionally practices with  them in their respective training three  years pass and the men fully complete  their training and become expert kung fu  fighters as they say their final  goodbyes to their master he gives them  some valuable intel on tien 2. the  tyrant is throwing a party in a few days  to celebrate his 45th birthday hence  that would be a perfect opportunity to  attack jin ying advises them to attack  tien 2 together and get used to the  fighter's black tiger style before  trying to finish him off the group  thanks him for his help over the years  after this they leave the school to  enact their revenge chen proposes they  return to town separately to observe any  new changes and avoid arousing suspicion  he disguises himself as a fortune teller  and re-enters the town as he arrives at  the tavern for a drink the tavern keeper  recognizes chen and quietly warns him  that tientu's top bodyguard juan is in  the room chen is amused by this and  walks over to one's table sitting with  the top guard while the other men stare  at him after conversing chen confidently  reveals to an unsuspecting juan that he  is the very same man his boss blinded  years ago the bodyguards swiftly attack  chen but he easily defeats them with his  quick-witted kicks and blows so much for  keeping a low profile juan also pounces  at chen and the duo engage in an intense  battle juan bombards him with several  punches but with the aid of his staff  chen dodges all of them ultimately chen  hits one with his staff which knocks him  back juan is startled by the blind man's  expert abilities and leaves the tavern  with his men soon after shortly  afterwards juan returns to the mansion  and hires a pair of fighting masters lin  and lou to defeat chen before tientu's  birthday the next morning wei also  arrives in town and visits the tavern he  is welcomed by the shop owner who leads  him to a special table upstairs to enjoy  a drink right then juan arrives with his  men and chases all the customers away  from the tavern while way hides upstairs  observing the group from the elevated  ground meanwhile juan orders the men to  remain still and to not make a sound as  they wait to ambush a blind chan just as  chen enters lynn shoots an iron ball at  him but way saves him by pushing a table  from upstairs to stop the shot the sound  alerts chen to the surrounding men and a  fight ensues juan and his men launch a  series of rapid attacks but the two  cripples dodged their blows and expertly  defeat them seeing this a cautious wand  signals his men to stop fighting and  retreats to the mansion that evening way  is attacked from behind by lou but the  deaf man spots him using a mirror  attached to his neck and dodges the  strike after a brief fight wade defeats  and kills lou while one of juan's men  observes from a distance a few minutes  later the witness shows one lou's corpse  and reveals that way was the one who  killed the skilled fighter the news  greatly disturbs juan prompting him to  devise a plan to kill the cripples  geez that night one and his men find  chen and way at the tavern one attacks  way and an intense fight ensues chen  tries to join the fight but wandsman  beat drums to hinder his hearing the  drumming sound confuses chen as he  frantically waves his rod around hitting  nothing but air fortunately wei comes to  his aid and charges towards the drumming  man when the noisy sounds stop chen  regains his composure and joins the  fight juan and his men rush the duo with  multiple sword swings but the cripples  easily disarm them using their  heightened senses way hits several  guards in the face with his fists while  chen wards them off by skillfully  swinging his staff juan and his men are  stopped by mr cho one of tiantu's old  friends who had just arrived in town for  his birthday this party's starting to  pop off cho a veteran fighter sends the  men away and assures them that he can  single-handedly defeat the duo when they  leave cho admits that he feels terrible  about fighting a pair of cripples and  makes them a proposition he offers them  three free punches and kicks before they  even start fighting just to even the  playing field instantly the duo accepts  the offer with whey punching and kicking  him three times however a sturdy cho  barely flinches chen also tries to knock  him down by delivering multiple attacks  and even a high kick but cho once again  remains unmoved right then akui and yi  emerge from the tavern's secret room and  join the others akui asks cho for his  free attacks and the boastful veteran  obliges akui strikes cho three times  with his fists but the latter remains  unaffected however when aku kicks him  with his iron feet cho is left brutally  injured he tries to fight the group but  they dodge his attacks after which he  succumbs to his injuries and 